  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.0\n\n### Features\n- Link targets import as bookmarks (`Block.Bookmarks`), so a `#name` link navigates: the `id` of a paragraph or heading names it, the `id` of a container (list item, cell, quote) names its first paragraph, and an `a` element's `name` or `id` names the paragraph it sits in.\n\n### Fixes\n- Attribute values kept their character references verbatim, so `<a href=\"?a=1&amp;b=2\">` imported a link to `?a=1&amp;b=2` and `alt=\"Tom &amp; Jerry\"` kept the `&amp;`. Values are now decoded the same way as text, for the reader's own attributes and for the values an `IHtmlTagHandler` receives through `HtmlTagAttributes`. A bare `&` that starts no known reference stays as it is.\n- A quoted `font-family` list lost only its first and last quote, so `font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial` imported the family `Segoe UI', Arial`. Each family is now unquoted on its own and the list is joined the way the model spells one (`Segoe UI,Arial`). An empty list leaves the family unset instead of setting it to an empty name.\n- A full page's `<title>` imported as the document's first paragraph, because the tag was passed through like `<head>` and `<body>`. Its content is now skipped the way `<script>` and `<style>` content is.\n- `font-style: oblique` imported as `FontStyle.Italic`, and the angle form `oblique 10deg` was ignored. Both now map to `FontStyle.Oblique`.\n- A `>` inside a quoted attribute value ended the tag, so `<a href=\"?q=a>b\">` linked to `?q=a` and imported the rest of the tag as text. A quote right after `=` now holds the tag open until the matching quote closes the value.",
  "repository": {
